34,2,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I have some concerning news. Our development budget is nearly a quarter lower than expected, and we must now pay for floor space fitting out from this same limited fund. We must be very cautious.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The budget is a constraint, but the real risk is inefficiency. My findings show that the call-back trial actually reduced readmissions by 20%, yet it was abandoned. Why waste money on new ideas when proven ones were buried?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I'm worried about our capacity. We have nine unfilled nursing posts and rising agency costs. While midwifery has some slack, our physiotherapy staff are leaving for the city. We cannot launch a program that adds pressure to already exhausted teams.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"I've got some bad news too! The car park fills up by eleven and rooms are packed from mid-morning. Plus, the booking system is missing a lot of data because it only tracks fixed appointments. We're already full!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems we have many hurdles to clear. I found that our past joint ventures failed when no one took ownership of the budget, and our legal agreements with outside partners can take over a year to finalize.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, that is a critical point. Combined with the fact that off-site contacts generate no regional fund tariffs, any program relying on outside partnerships or remote work could become a financial drain we cannot afford.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, exactly. If we chase ""partnerships"" that don't pay and ignore the 20% readmission drop we already achieved, we're just being negligent. We should prioritize programs with a proven track record of patient impact.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, I agree that patient impact is key, but we must be realistic. If we implement a program that requires heavy nursing or physiotherapy input, we risk further burnout and more staff leaving for the city.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, that's true! But even if we have the staff, where will the patients go? If the rooms are already full by mid-morning, we can't just add more people without the whole place seizing up!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"It is a bit worrying, isn't it? If we rush into a partnership without a clear owner or a signed agreement, we may find ourselves in a very difficult position once the initial excitement fades. We must be gentle with our planning.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"Given the budget cuts and the lack of tariffs for off-site work, we must prioritize a program that is on-site and financially self-sustaining. We cannot risk a deficit in twelve months.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, then the choice is simple. We need a program that utilizes existing on-site resources and has a demonstrated effect on patient health. Let's not ignore the evidence of what actually works just to be ""innovative.""","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, I agree, but ""existing resources"" are stretched thin. We must avoid any program that relies on ward nurses or physiotherapists. Perhaps we can look for something that utilizes the slack in the midwifery rota instead?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, that's a great idea! If we use the midwifery slack, it might help. But we still have to solve the parking and room problem. We can't just add more appointments to a system that's already crashing!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with Midori's kindness toward our staff. However, we must also be careful not to rely on outside surgeries or clinics unless the agreements are already signed. A year of waiting is a long time indeed.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"It seems we are converging on a strict set of criteria: on-site delivery to ensure tariff revenue, minimal reliance on overstretched nursing or therapy staff, and a low impact on our physical space. We must be pragmatic.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shion,,"Pragmatism is only useful if it's based on results. We must select the candidate that aligns with these constraints while offering a proven benefit to patients, rather than another experiment destined for the archives.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I hope we can find a candidate that fits all these needs. If we can support our patients while protecting our staff's wellbeing, it will be a true success for everyone. I'm ready to see the options.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm ready too! I just hope the candidates aren't all ""big"" projects. We really need something that doesn't make the parking lot a nightmare or break our booking system. Let's see what we've got!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I agree. Let us look upon the candidates with a patient heart and a careful eye. I hope we find a path that is stable, sustainable, and truly supportive of all who will touch it.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
