59,3,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Looking at the options, A and D are off-site or involve outside providers, meaning no tariff revenue. B requires new space and physiotherapy staff, both of which we lack. Option C seems the most viable.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, I agree. A and D are essentially the ""off-site"" failures I warned about—unfunded and prone to the same gaps as the shared nursing round. C is the only logical choice that fits our constraints.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, @Shion, I agree. Option C is the only one that aligns with our staffing reality. Since the midwifery rota has slack, it won't overburden our exhausted nurses or physiotherapists. It's a sustainable choice for our team.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, I agree! Option C uses the midwifery slack, which is great. It's also a scheduled service, so it's easier to track than the ""invisible"" work that's currently breaking our booking system. It seems the safest bet!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with you all. Option C is a lovely choice. Since it is run jointly by our own departments, we can ensure the budget and responsibilities are clearly shared from the start, avoiding any future misunderstandings.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,It is rare that we find such unanimous agreement. Option C is the only candidate that secures our financial future through on-site tariffs while respecting our current staffing and space limitations. It is the most responsible choice.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shion,,"It is the only choice that doesn't ignore our reality. While it lacks the specific readmission data of the call-back trial, it is far superior to gambling on unfunded, off-site experiments that we know will fail.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Midori,,"I feel very relieved that we've found a solution that protects our staff. By utilizing the available capacity in midwifery, we can provide wonderful care without risking further burnout for our other teams. It's a balanced approach.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"I'm relieved too! Since it's scheduled, we can manage the flow of people better. It's the best way to help new parents without making the parking lot or the booking system totally explode!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"It is a comfort to see us all in such agreement. By choosing a path that is stable and supportive of our own people, we ensure that this program will truly flourish and bring joy to the families it serves.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I believe we have done our due diligence. Option C is the only proposal that is financially sustainable, operationally feasible, and respectful of our staff's limits. I am fully committed to this choice.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shion,,"I concur. While I would have preferred a program with a proven track record of reducing readmissions, Option C is the only one that doesn't actively invite failure. It is the only logical decision.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Midori,,I concur as well. It is the only option that allows us to grow while remaining kind to our staff. I am happy to cast my vote for Option C.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm all in for Option C too! It's the only one that doesn't feel like it'll jam up the whole hospital. Let's go with the one that actually fits in our day!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I agree completely. Option C is a gentle and sustainable path that protects our staff and our partnerships. I am very happy to cast my vote for the Perinatal Support Service.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"Since we are all in agreement on the financial, staffing, and spatial merits of the Perinatal Support Service, I see no reason to delay. I cast my vote for Option C.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shion,,I cast my vote for Option C. It is the only choice that respects the constraints of our reality without blindly repeating the mistakes of the past.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Midori,,"I cast my vote for Option C. It is the most balanced choice, ensuring we provide excellent care while truly looking after the wellbeing of our staff.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I cast my vote for Option C! It's the only one that won't make the parking lot a nightmare or crash our booking system. Let's make it happen!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I cast my vote for Option C. It is a wonderful choice that ensures stability and kindness for everyone involved. I am glad we could find such a harmonious agreement.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
